Subject: [PATCH 89/94] arm64: dts: qcom: sdm660-hiby-rs6: Add stock's DDR
 floor per CPU frequency

Stock raises DDR with the CPU clock, before its BWMON sees the traffic:
the "mincpubw" devbw client (APSS -> EBI, active-only) runs the
devfreq-cpufreq governor ("cpufreq" in init.qcom.post_boot.sh), which
maps each cluster's frequency through cpu-to-dev-map-0 (pwrcl) and
cpu-to-dev-map-4 (perfcl) and votes the highest result. A frequency
takes the first map entry at or above it, the last one past the end
(governor_cpufreq.c cpu_to_dev_freq(), the same loop in the stock
kernel's devfreq_cpufreq_get_freq()).

  pwrcl  kHz  <=633600: 762  <=1401600: 1571  <=1881600: 2929  MiB/s
  perfcl kHz <=1113600: 762  <=1401600: 2086  <=1747200: 2929
             <=2150400: 3879 <=2457600: 6881

Put each OPP's floor in opp-peak-kBps, in the units of the CPU BWMON
table (MiB/s * 1048576 / 1000, the same RPM request as stock's
ib = MiB/s * 2^20):

  pwrcl   300.0- 633.6 MHz   762 MiB/s   799014 kB/s
          902.4-1401.6 MHz  1571 MiB/s  1647312 kB/s
         1536.0-1843.2 MHz  2929 MiB/s  3071279 kB/s
  perfcl  300.0-1113.6 MHz   762 MiB/s   799014 kB/s
               1401.6 MHz   2086 MiB/s  2187329 kB/s
               1747.2 MHz   2929 MiB/s  3071279 kB/s
         1958.4-2150.4 MHz  3879 MiB/s  4067426 kB/s
               2208.0 MHz   6881 MiB/s  7215251 kB/s

qcom-cpufreq-hw votes it on the cluster's APSS -> EBI path when it
switches frequency; the interconnect core takes the highest peak of
the two clusters and the BWMON, as msm_bus did for stock's clients.

